Privacy Policy for ErrorLens
Effective date: April 22, 2026

ErrorLens is a browser extension that helps users understand technical errors by turning error messages into plain-English explanations, likely causes, and suggested next steps.

Information ErrorLens may process
ErrorLens may process:

error text that users paste into the extension
text that users intentionally select on a webpage and send to the extension
user-created custom rules
recent error history saved by the user
basic extension preferences
How ErrorLens uses information
ErrorLens uses this information only to provide its core functionality, including:

analyzing error messages
showing explanations and suggested next steps
saving recent lookups for reuse
storing custom rules created by the user
remembering basic extension settings
Data storage
ErrorLens may store recent errors, custom rules, and preferences locally in the browser using Chrome extension storage so the extension can function properly and improve usability.

Data sharing
ErrorLens does not sell user data.

ErrorLens does not use user data for advertising.

ErrorLens does not use or transfer user data for purposes unrelated to the extension's single purpose.

ErrorLens does not use or transfer user data to determine creditworthiness or for lending purposes.

Third-party services
ErrorLens does not transfer user data to third parties except when necessary to provide the extension's core functionality, if applicable.

User control
Users control what text they paste into ErrorLens and what page content they choose to analyze.

Users can clear saved extension data, including recent history and custom rules, at any time.

Security
Reasonable steps are taken to limit access to data and to use it only for the intended purpose of the extension.

Changes to this policy
This privacy policy may be updated from time to time. Any changes will be reflected on this page.

